    <string name="private_banner_body">Pages you visit here are not saved to history, and cookies, site data and cache are erased when you close the private session. Private tabs run in a separate window and process.</string>
    <string name="private_banner_limits">Private browsing does not make you anonymous: websites, your network and your internet provider can still see your activity. Downloaded files stay on your device.</string>
    <string name="private_info_full">What private browsing does:\n• Runs in its own window, process and web-data folder, separate from regular tabs.\n• Never writes visited pages to history, and never saves tabs.\n• Erases cookies, site storage and cache when the private session is closed (and clears leftovers the next time one starts).\n• Hides pages from screenshots and the recent-apps preview.\n\nWhat it does not do:\n• It does not hide your activity from websites, your network administrator or your internet provider.\n• Files you download are kept on your device, and Android\'s download list may show them.\n• Bookmarks and settings changes are disabled inside private windows.</string>
